-- title:
--   Chart functions read in a component of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly over $L$, and let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), assumed nonzero. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$, let $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension one and geometrically integral, and let $i$ be a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ from $c$ to the base change along $A \to k$ of the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), with underlying morphism $i.1$ a closed immersion. Then for every $\xi \in C$ whose closure is all of $C$, every field $F$ with a $k$-algebra structure, every $\mathrm{Mdl} :$ [`AlgebraicCurve.CurveModel k F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_CurveModel.html#L23) (a smooth proper integral $k$-scheme with an identification of $F$ with its function field and a bijection of its closed points with the places of $F/k$), and every isomorphism $e : \mathrm{Mdl}.C \cong C$ with $e.\mathrm{hom}$ followed by $c$ equal to $\mathrm{Mdl}.\mathrm{toBase}$, there exist: a valuation subring $V$ of $K$ containing the image of $A$ and sending $\mathfrak{m}_A$ into the nonunits of $V$, such that for every polynomial $P$ over $A$ with nonzero reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$; an $A$-algebra structure on $V$ compatible with the inclusion into $K$; the inclusion of the $A$-subalgebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) generated by $j$ into $V$; the fact that the image $z$ of $\xi$ under $i.1$ followed by the first pullback projection lies in the open image of the $j$-finite chart $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236); a ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from the stalk of that integral model at $z$ onto $V$ carrying the germ at $z$ of each chart function $a$ to $a$ itself; a minimal prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of $k \otimes_A V$; a $k$-algebra isomorphism $\Psi : F \simeq \operatorname{Frac}\big((k \otimes_A V)/\mathfrak{q}\big)$; and nonemptiness of the preimage in $\mathrm{Mdl}.C$ of the $j$-finite chart along $e.\mathrm{hom}$ followed by $i.1$ and the pullback projection; such that for every $a \in$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), the element of $F$ obtained by pulling $a$ back along that composite, taking its germ at the generic point of $\mathrm{Mdl}.C$ in the function field and transporting it through $\mathrm{Mdl}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, is sent by $\Psi$ to the class of $1 \otimes a$ in $\operatorname{Frac}\big((k \otimes_A V)/\mathfrak{q}\big)$.
--
--   This identifies the function field of an irreducible component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ with the fraction field of $(k \otimes_A V)/\mathfrak{q}$, where $V$ is the valuation ring of $K$ attached to the component, and records that the identification reads the $j$-finite chart functions as the classes of $1 \otimes a$. It is the form in which the component's function field is used in the study of the Igusa components and of the $\infty$-branch $q$-expansions, and it is cited by the statements producing curve models of the components together with the comparison of the two components and their crossings.
